// `#error "msg"` is a compile-time diagnostic. Reached in live code — a bare
// top-level one here; in practice the taken `else` arm of an `inline if OS == { … }`
// on an unsupported target — the compiler emits `msg` as an error and stops. In a
// NON-taken comptime arm it is pruned before it can fire, which is how std/c.sx and
// std/posix.sx guard their per-OS tables.

#error("compilation intentionally halted: the #error directive was reached.");

main :: () {
    // Never reached — the #error above stops compilation first.
}
